# Enemy patrol cutter ? NATIVE 8? (2026-08-20): a gasbag envelope
# tethered on struts above an enclosed one-room cabin ? twin 4x4 boiler
# engines on the cabin floor, a standing 4x7 control panel starboard (a
# DRIVER mans it and flies the ship; enemy ships are crewed, never
# automated), an 8-tall door in the port wall, a 2x6 stern pusher, 6x2
# lift props under the keel, and one 2x8 turret slung beneath on a
# strut, manned by a GUNNER. Crew stand INSIDE the ship, not on its
# roof. The door spawns closed ? boarders open it with F, or shoot it
# out. Component footprints are the surveyed true sizes; outputs and
# masses are ratings (BlockDB.FOOTPRINT_8X), so this flies exactly like
# its slab-era ancestor (frozen at tests/fixtures/hulk_1x.ship).
#
# NOTE the parser rule: comments are "# " (hash-space) or a bare "#".
# A grid row may START with '#' (hull) ? that is the whole reason for
# the rule.

# THE HEADER VOCABULARY (Q-T, 2026-09-02) — the worked example. These lines are
# what the spawn code used to assume: this file is a vessel, its role is a
# gunboat, and killing it in a Dive pays 35 coins at depth 1 (exactly what
# DiveRun.KIND_COIN["hulk"] already said — the number moved into the file it
# describes, it did not change).
name Patrol Cutter
kind vessel
role gunboat
bounty 35
origin 24 32
